$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Alkyl iodide 18 (1 equiv) was stirred in 3:2 pentane / ether to give a
0.1 M solution. The solution was cooled to -78 °C and a 1.8 M
tert-butyllithium solution in pentane (2.2 equiv) was added by a syringe.
After 10-15 min at -78 °C, the appropriate β,®-unsaturated aldehyde (1.3-
1.8 equiv) was added by a syringe. Once TLC analysis indicated conversion
to allylic alcohol (ca. 1 h) the reaction was quenched with sat. NaHCO3
and allowed to warm to 23 °C. The resulting mixture was extracted with
ether. The combined extracts were washed with brine, dried (MgSO4),
filtered, and concentrated to give the corresponding allylic alcohol.
(E)-1-(syn-7-Allylnorborn-2-en-7-yl)pent-3-en-2-ol (19a). Yield 22 mg,
90%. TLC Rf = 0.42, (3:1 hexanes / ethyl acetate); 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 5.96-5.90 (m, 2H), 5.78-5.60 (m, 2H), 5.54-5.42 (m, 1H), 5.00-
4.90 (m, 2H), 4.27-4.22 (m, 1H), 2.56 (br s, 1H), 2.44 (br s, 1H), 2.35
(dd, J = 14.3, 7.0 Hz, 1H), 2.31 (dd, J = 14.3, 7.7 Hz, 1H), 1.91-1.75
(m, 2H), 1.70 (dd, J = 6.2, 1.5 Hz, 3H), 1.54 (dd, J = 14.7, 7.0 Hz, 1H),
1.44 (dd J = 14.7, 5.1 Hz, 1H), 1.27 (br, 1H), 0.97-0.90 (m, 2H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 137.8, 135.5, 134.6, 133.9, 126.1, 115.5, 71.1, 60.6,
48.1, 47.6, 37.8, 33.9, 23.2, 23.1, 17.6; IR (film) 3375, 3057, 2959,
2917, 2880, 1636, 1446, 1329, 996, 967 cm-1. HRMS (CI+ w/NH4) m/z calcd
for C15H24N ([M+NH4-H2O]+) 218.1909, obsd 218.1916.
