$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the vinylogous aldol
reaction of Brassard's diene and aromatic aldehydes:Under N2 atmosphere
in a dry Schlenk tube, a mixture of Ti(OiPr)4 (0.2 mmol) and (R)-BINOL
(0.2 mmol) was stirred in THF (16 mL) at room temperature for 20 min.
Then to this mixture was added H2O (7.2 μL, 0.2 mmol) with a syringe.
After another 20 min, anhydrous LiCl (8.6 mg, 0.2 mmol) kept in a Schlenk
tube was quickly added bottle to bottle under N2 atmosphere. After
stirring for 30 min, 8 mL of the catalyst solution was transferred to
another Schlenk tube and the aldehyde (1 mmol) and Brassard's diene 4
(2.5 mmol) was added successively. After stirring for 40 h at room
temperature, the reaction solution was cooled to 0°C and quenched with
five drops of 1M HCl. After stirring for additional 15 min, the mixture
was neutralized with saturated NaHCO3. After usual workup, the residue
was purified by chromatography on silica gel to afford the aldol product.
(2Z,6E)-ethyl 3-ethoxy-5-hydroxy-7-phenylhepta-2,6-dienoate (5l), as a
colorless oil, yield 71% after column chromatography (acetone/petroleum
ether = 1/12). [α]D19 = + 6.4 (c = 0.08, CH2Cl2); 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.27-7.32 (m, 4H), 6.63 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 2H), 6.63 (dd, J =
15.6 Hz, 6.4 Hz, 2H), 5.10 (s, 1H), 4.53-4.55 (m, 1H;), 4.15-4.23 (m,
2H), 4.10 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 2.65 (br, 1H), 2.48-2.50 (m, 2H), 1.33 (t,
J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 1.24 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
167.3, 165.4, 136.5, 130.8, 130.7, 128.8, 128.7, 127.9, 126.8, 99.0,
70.6, 67.7, 59.7, 43.1, 15.5, 14.4; ESI-HRMS: (M+Na)+, calcd. for C17 H22
O4 Na: 313.1416, found: 313.1430; Enantiomeric excess was determined to
be 90% with the (E) isomer of 5l (determined by HPLC using chiralcel OD-H
column, hexane/2-propanol = 9/1, λ = 254 nm, 30°C, 0.7 mL/min, tmajor =
31.1 min, tminor = 41.3 min).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (90% ee), Mukaiyama-Aldol reaction; Brassard's diene used
(stage 4), in-situ generated catalyst (stage 1-3)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mild and Highly Enantioselective Vinylogous Aldol Reaction of Brassard's
Diene with Aromatic Aldehydes by Combined Lewis Acid Catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wang, Guowei; Zhao, Jinfeng; Zhou, Yuhan; Wang, Baomin; Qu, Jingping
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2010), 75(15), 5326-5329

