$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Identification of the mono-complex Rh2(OAc)4 iPrNHC Complex 27 (6.0 mg,
5.00×10-3 mmol, 4.5 mol %) was weighted into a flamed dried round bottom
flask equipped with a condenser and under argon atmosphere. t-Amylalcohol
(0.3 mL), phenylboronic acid (27.00 mg, 0.22 mmol) and KO t Bu (2.80 mg,
0.025 mmol, 10 mol %) were successively added, the resulting suspension
was stirred at room temperature for 15 min. after which the corresponding
4-MeC6H5COH (0.11 mmol) were added. The resulting mixture was stirred at
90 °C for 1 h. The reaction mixture was concentrated under reduced
pressure and the residue was purified by preparative thin layer
chromatography (ethyl acetate/hexane), yielding the desired secondary
alcohol 16 quantitatively as a slightly yellow oil and a red-wine colored
solid (3.0 mg, 75 % based on the initial amount of 27 used) which was
identified as the Rh2(OAc)4 iPrNHC. The mono-complex Rh2(OAc)4 iPrNHC
(1.00 mg, 1.25×10-3 mmol, 1 mol %) was reused in a similar reaction
affording the secondary alcohol 16 in 95 % isolated yield. 1H NMR (C7D8)
δ (ppm) = 7.09-6.97 (m, toluene), 6.60 (s, 2H), 4.28 (s), 3.27-3.24 (m,
4H), 2.11-2.07 (toluene), 1.31 (s, 12H), 1.18 (d, 12H, J = 9.2 Hz), 1.06
(d, 12H, J = 9.0 Hz); 13C NMR (C7D8) δ (ppm) = 188.20, 145.61, 122.79,
28.10, 25.06, 22.83, 22.60.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Axial Coordination of NHC Ligands on Dirhodium(II) Complexes: Generation
of a New Family of Catalysts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Trindade, Alexandre F.; Gois, Pedro M. P.; Veiros, Luis F.; Andre,
Vavecnia; Duarte, M. Teresa; Afonso, Carlos A. M.; Caddick, Stephen;
Cloke, F. Geoffrey N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2008), 73(11), 4076-4086

