$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for N-O cleavage: To a solution of
(3R,6R)-6-methyl-2-phenyl-3-propyl-3,6-dihydro-2H-1,2-oxazine-4-carbaldehyde
(4a) in MeOH was treated with NaBH4 (4 equiv) at 0 oC. Then the mixture
was stirred at 0 oC for 1 hour and quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl
solution, extracted with ethyl acetate three times. The organic extracts
were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo after
filtration. The residue was dissolved in MeOH, treated with zinc (20
equiv) and HCl (40 equiv 1 M). The mixture was stirred at room
temperature until TLC indicated complete reaction, then treated with
saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution until pH > 9. The mixture was extracted
with ethyl acetate three times and the combined organic phases were
washed with brine. The organic extracts were dried over anhydrous Na2SO4,
and concentrated in vacuo after filtration. The residue was purified on
silica gel (PE : EtOAc = 1 : 1) to give
(R,E)-2-((R)-1-(phenylamino)butyl)pent-2-ene-1,4-diol as a solid. White
solid, yield (91% for 2 steps). Purified by flash chromatograph column
(PE: EtOAc = 1 : 1). The enantiomeric excess was determined by chiral
HPLC using a Daicel Chiralpak AD column (hexane/i-PrOH = 90/10); flow
rate 1.0 mL/min; τmajor = 10.5min, τminor = 14.9min, ee >99%. [α]D 25 =
-65.2 (c = 1.0, CH2Cl2). 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 7.16 (t, J = 7.4, 8.2
Hz, 2H), 6.73 (t, J = 7.3, 7.3 Hz, 1H), 6.58 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 5.57
(d, J = 9.1 Hz, 1H), 4.74-4.82 (m, 1H), 4.25 (t, J = 6.0, 8.2 Hz, 1H),
4.09 (d, J = 4.1 Hz, 2H), 2.61 (s, 1H), 1.73-1.82 (m, 1H), 1.62-1.71 (m,
1H), 1.37 - 1.55 (m, 2H), 1.32 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H), 0.98 (t, J = 7.3, 7.3
Hz, 3H) 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ 147.8, 141.8, 132.1, 129.4, 118.1,
113.6, 64.8, 63.8, 54.0, 38.3, 23.9, 20.0, 14.1 FT-IR (film): ν 3346,
3052, 2961, 2929, 2871, 1602, 1504, 1456, 1429, 1371, 1319, 1259, 1179,
1154, 1128, 1103, 1058, 992, 868, 750, 693, 512 cm-1 HRMS (APCI) [M+H]+:
Calculated for [C21H21F3NO2]+: 250.1807 found: 250.1790
