$DATUM (Z)-3-Hydroxy-4-phenyl-5-trifluoromethylnon-4-ene (2b). A solution of
enol ether 3 (220 mg, 1 mmol), n-butyllithium (1.3 mL of a 1.6 M solution
in hexanes, 2.1 mmol), and TMEDA (490 mg, 2.1 mmol) in hexane (10 mL),
after addition of propanal (70 mg, 1.2 mmol), afforded, after workup and
purification, the alcohol 2b (232 mg, 83%). 19F NMR δ -55.7 (s); 1H NMR δ
0.71 (t, J = 7 Hz, 3 H), 0.93 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 3 H), 1.0-1.4 (m, 8 H), 1.6
(broad s, 1 H, OH), 4.75 (m, 1 H), 7.2 (m, 5 H, C6H5); 13C NMR δ 10.3,
13.5, 22.5, 28.7, 29.5, 31.4, 71.8 (q, 4 J = 2.6 Hz), 124.8 (q, 1 J = 278
Hz, CF3), 127.6, 128.1, 129.0, 130.2 (q, 2 JCF = 28 Hz, C-CF3), 135.9,
149.6. Anal. Calcd For C16H21F3O: C, 67.13; H, 7.34. Found: C, 66.79; H,
7.66.
