$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure 1 for Preparation of Enynyl
Alcohols: To a solution of n-BuLi (1.6 M in hexanes, 10 mmol) in THF (20
mL) was added the corresponding enyne (10 mmol) at -78°C under argon. The
resulting reaction mixture was stirred at the same temperature for 30 min
and was then allowed to warm at -20°C over 5 min. Ketone or aldehyde (11
mmol) was then added at -78°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 30
min at -78°C and was then allowed to reach room temperature and was
stirred further until completion of reaction as monitored by TLC. The
mixture was quenched with satd NH4Cl solution and extracted twice with
Et2O. The combined organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4. After
evaporation the crude product was purified by flash chromatography
(Cyclohexane/EtOAc) to afford the title compound.
3-(Cyclohex-1-enyl)-1-p-tolylprop-2-yn-1-ol (IV): Prepared following the
general procedure 1 in 91 % yield (1.92 g) from 1 g of
1-ethynylcyclohexene and 4-methylbenzaldehyde (1.1 equiv.) after elution
with Cyclohexane/EtOAc. Colorless oil: Rf = 0.8 (Cyclohexane/EtOAc 20 %);
IR (CHCl3) ν max 3389, 3020, 3010, 2940, 2863, 2185, 1716, 1634, 1603,
1571, 1513, 1449, 1409, 1359, 1310, 1280, 1265, 1222, 1177, 1115, 1076,
1046, 950 cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.62 (m, 4 H), 2.13 (m,4 H),
2.31 (d, 1 H, J = 6.2 Hz), 2.36 (s, 3 H), 5.53 (d, 1 H, J = 6.2 Hz), 6.16
(m, 1 H), 7.18 (m, 2 H), 7.44 (m, 2 H) ; 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 21.1,
21.1, 21.4, 25.6, 29.1, 64.8, 86.2, 88.3, 120.1, 126.6, 129.2, 135.5,
138.0, 141.9; MS (ESI) m/z (%) 249 (100, M+.+Na), 209 (27, M+.-OH); HR-MS
249.1318 (C16H18O+Na calcd 249.1250).
