$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-(2-Furyl)-3-hydroxy-2-methylenepropanenitrile (19d). Purification by
column chromatography (4:1 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a desired compound 19d
(76.4 mg, 51%) as a yellow liquid. Spectral data were identical to those
previously reported.9 TLC: R f 0.50 (1:1 hexane/EtOAc). 1H-NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.44 (m, 1H), 6.44 (m, 1H), 6.40 (dd, 1H, J = 3.2, 1.6 Hz),
6.20 (d, 1H, J = 1.6 Hz), 6.15 (d, 1H, J = 1.6 Hz), 5.37 (d, 1H, J = 5.6
Hz), 2.38 (d, 1H, J = 5.6 Hz). 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 151.6, 143.6,
131.4, 123.6, 116.8, 111.0, 109.0, 68.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction, 1-butyl-3-methyltriazolium hexafluorophosphate
as solvent gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 1,3-Dialkyl-1,2,3-triazolium Ionic Liquids and Their
Applications to the Baylis-Hillman Reaction
