$DATUM 2-(Furan-2-ylhydroxymethyl)acrylonitrile (Table 3, entry 3). A solution
of furfuraldehyde (340 mg, 3.54 mmol), acrylonitrile (225 mg, 4.25 mmol),
quinuclidine (98.4 mg, 0.88 mmol), and methanol (85.0 mg, 2.65 mmol) was
stirred for 20 min at room temperature. Column chromatography on silica
(hexane/Et2O 2:1) gave 531 mg (78%) of the product as an orange liquid
2-(Furan-2-ylhydroxymethyl)acrylonitrile, yield 531 mg (78%) (Rf = 0.3):
IR (neat) 3418, 2230, 1625, 1502, 1397 cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 2.45 (br s,
1H), 5.37 (s, 1H), 6.15 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 1H), 6.20 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 1H),
6.40 (dd, J = 3.1 Hz, J = 1.7 Hz, 1H), 6.44 (dd, J = 3.1 Hz, J = 0.9 Hz,
1H), 7.44 (dd, J = 1.7 Hz, J = 0.9 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 67.9,
108.8, 110.8, 116.6, 123.5, 131.2, 143.5, 151.6; MS m/z 149 (40) [M+],
132 (90), 97 (100), 53 (9); HRMS (EI) calcd for C8H7NO2 149.0476, found
149.0477.
