$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the indium-mediated
addition of 1 to 2. 3-Benzenesulfonyl-2-methyl-1-phenyl-2-vinylpropanol
(3a). Table 1, Entry 1: To a stirred solution of the C5 chloroallylic
sulfone (E)-1a (0.31 g, 1.25 mmol) in THF (2 mL) were added 2a (0.16 g,
1.50 mmol), Indium (0.16 g, 1.38 mmol), and H2O (8 mL). The mixture was
stirred at reflux for 2.5 h, and cooled to room temperature. The mixture
was then diluted with CH2Cl2, washed with 1 M HCl, dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude
product was purified by washing with hexanes to give 3a (0.39 g, 1.23
mmol, anti:syn = 13:1) in 98% yield as a white solid.
1-Benzenesulfonyl-3-hydroxy-2-methyl-2-vinyl-4-octene (3k). Table 1,
Entry 11: The reaction of (E)-1a (0.41 g, 1.69 mmol), 2k (0.20 g, 2.03
mmol), and indium (0.21 g, 1.86 mmol) in THF/H2O (2 mL/8 mL) at reflux
for 2 h gave 3k (0.4 g, 1.30 mmol, anti:syn = 2:1) in 77% yield. Data for
anti-3k: 1H NMR δ 0.87 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H), 1.32 (s, 3H), 1.38 (sext, J =
7.3 Hz, 2H), 2.00 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 2.35 (br s, 1H), 3.17 (d, J = 14.2
Hz, 1H), 3.42 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 4.19 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 5.04 (d, J
= 17.6 Hz, 1H), 5.13 (d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1H), 5.37 (dd, J = 16.5, 7.8 Hz,
1H), 5.69 (dt, Jd = 16.5, Jt = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 5.93 (dd, J = 17.6, 10.8 Hz,
1H), 7.50-7.66 (m, 3H), 7.86-7.93 (m, 2H) ppm; 13C NMR δ 13.6, 19.3,
22.2, 34.4, 45.4, 62.5, 77.4, 115.5, 127.7, 129.2, 133.6, 134.5, 135.6,
140.2, 141.3 ppm; IR (KBr) 3505, 1448, 1307, 1149 cm-1; HRMS (CI+) cacld
for C17H23O3S 307.1368, found 307.1368. Data for syn-3k: 1H NMR δ 0.86
(t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H), 1.23 (s, 3H), 3.16 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 3.45 (d, J
= 14.2 Hz, 1H), 4.23 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H), 5.08 (d, J = 17.6 Hz, 1H), 5.12
(d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1H), 5.40 (dd, J = 16.5, 7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.05 (dd, J =
17.6, 10.8 Hz, 1H) ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 2:1 anti:syn
