$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAS_Reaction_Number
$DATUM 31-320-CAS-6592660
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):STEPS
$DATUM 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):STAGES
$DATUM 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):PRO(1):YIELD
$DATUM 82
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):RGT(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 280-57-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
Baylis-Hillman adducts 1a, 1c-f. A mixture of acrylate (or methyl
vinylketone) (100 mmol), aldehyde (130 mmol) and DABCO
(1,4-diazabicyclo[2.2.2]octane) (20 mmol) was stirred for 3-5 days and
then diluted with EtOAc. The reaction was washed twice with 1M HCl, dried
over MgSO4 and concentrated. The crude was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel using hexanes-ethyl acetate as eluent. Ethyl
3-hydroxy-3-phenyl-2-methylidene-propanoate 1f: 82% colorless oil. 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.30 (t, J= 7.0 Hz, 3H), 3.10 (bs, 1H, OH). 4.17 (q,
J= 7.0 Hz, 2H), 5.52 (s, 1H), 5.85 (s, 1H), 6.25 (s, 1H), 7.25-7.40 (m,
5H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) 6 60.8, 72.7, 125.2, 126.6, 127.6, 128.2,
141.5, 142.4, 166.1
