$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative general procedure for the
addition of acetylene derivatives to aldehydes: Chiral ligand Fam-1
(0.0554 mmol, 20 mg) was weighed into a pre-dried flask which was
attached to a vacuum-argon line. After vacuum, the flask was filled with
argon and freshly distilled THF (1.15 mL, dried over
sodium-benzophenone), Et2Zn (0.665 mmol, 1M solution in hexanes) and
phenylacetylene (0.776 mmol, 85.2 μL) were added. Thishomogenous mixture
was stirred at room temperature for 2 hours. Then, freshly distilled
Ti(OiPr)4 (0.139 mmol, 41 μL) was added and this final mixture was
stirred for 1 hour. At the end of this period, reaction mixture was
cooled to 0 oC and aldehyde (0.554 mmol) was added and the reaction was
allowed to proceed for 5h at this temperature. Saturated ammonium
chloride (3 mL) was added to quench the reaction, and ethyl acetate (3x10
mL) was used for extraction. The organic phase was combined, dried over
Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified
by flash column chromatography on silica gel with hexane/ethyl acetate
(10:1) as the eluent to afford the propargylic alcohol. Enantiomeric
excess valus were determined by chiral HPLC.
3-Phenyl-1-(thiophen-2-yl)prop-2-yn-1-ol (16): 73 % isolated yield 96% ee
determined by HPLC analysis (Chiralcel OD-H column 10% IPA in hexanes,
flow rate = 1.0 mL/min, 254 nm). Retention time: tmajor= 11.3 min and
tminor= 21.1 min. [α]D 28 = + 20.7 (c= 1.07, CHCl3), lit5. [α]D = + 20
(c= 0.53, CHCl3). 1H NMR δ 7.41-7.39 (m, 2H, Ar-H), 7.25-7.21 (m, 4H,
Ar-H), 7.15 (d, J = 3.2 Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 6.91 (t, J = 4.2 Hz, 1H, Ar-H),
5.77 (br s, 1H), 2.27 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR δ 144.9, 131.8, 128.7, 128.3,
126.7, 126.0, 125.5, 122.3, 88.2, 86.0, 60.7
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 96% ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Fam-Ti Catalyzed Enantioselective Alkynylation of Aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Koyuncu, Hasan; Dogan, Oezdemir
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(17), 3477-3479

