$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Alkyl iodide 18 (1 equiv) was stirred in 3:2
pentane / ether to give a 0.1 M solution. The solution was cooled to -78
°C and a 1.8 M tert-butyllithium solution in pentane (2.2 equiv) was
added by a syringe. After 10-15 min at -78 °C, the appropriate
β,®-unsaturated aldehyde (1.3- 1.8 equiv) was added by a syringe. Once
TLC analysis indicated conversion to allylic alcohol (ca. 1 h) the
reaction was quenched with sat. NaHCO3 and allowed to warm to 23 °C. The
resulting mixture was extracted with ether. The combined extracts were
washed with brine, dried (MgSO4), filtered, and concentrated to give the
corresponding allylic alcohol.
(E)-1-(syn-7-(allyl)norborn-2-en-7-yl)-5-methylhex-3-en-2-ol (19b). Yield
215 mg, 88%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.96-5.90 (m, 2H), 5.78-5.66 (m,
1H), 5.61 (ddd, J = 15.4, 6.6, 0.7 Hz, 1H), 5.44 (ddd, J = 15.4, 7.3, 1.1
Hz, 1H), 4.98-4.92 (m, 2H), 4.25 (ddd, J = 7.3, 5.9, 1.1 Hz, 1H), 2.55
(br dd, J = 2.9, 2.9 Hz, 1H), 2.45 (br dd, J = 2.9, 2.9 Hz, 1H),
2.38-2.24 (m, 2H), 1.92-1.76 (m, 2H), 1.55 (dd, J = 14.7, 7.3 Hz, 1H),
1.46 (dd, J = 14.7, 5.9 Hz, 1H), 1.28 (br s, 1H), 1.00 (d, J = 6.6 Hz,
6H), 0.98-0.88 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 138.4, 137.8, 134.5,
134.0, 131.1, 115.5, 71.2, 60.6, 48.1, 47.6, 38.0, 34.0, 30.6, 23.2,
23.1, 22.1; IR (film) 3378, 3058, 2959, 2873, 1636, 1465, 1446, 1329, 971
cm-1. HRMS (EI+) m/z calcd for C17H25 ([M-OH]+) 229.1956, obsd 229.1952.
