$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of n-BuLi (3.40 mL of 1.6 M in hexane, 5.45 mmol) in
anhydrous THF (7 mL), at 0 °C, 5-methyl-2-furaldehyde 8 (0.45 mL, 4.54
mmol) in anhydrous THF (3 mL) was added dropwise. After 30 min stirring
at the same temperature the reaction mixture was partitioned between Et2O
(10 mL) and NH4Cl (8 mL). The layers were separated and the organic layer
was washed with brine (8 mL), dried with Na2SO4, and concentrated in
vacuo. The residue was purified by flash column chromatography (silica
gel, hexane:EtOAc = 10:1) to afford the desired alcohol (0.53 g, 70 %).
1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 6.07 (brs, 1H), 6.03 (brs, 1H), 4.51 (t, J =
4.2 Hz, 1H), 2.21 (s, 3H), 1.76 (m, 2H), 1.28 (m, 4H), 0.85 (t, J = 6.9
Hz, 3H) ppm; 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 155.1, 151.1, 106.2, 105.7,
67.4, 34.9, 27.6, 22.2, 13.7, 13.2 ppm.
