$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure A: Formation of alcohols via allyl
indium reagents s-Butyl lithium (1.0 M solution in hexanes, 3.0 eq.) was
added to a stirred solution of allyl ethyl ether (3.0 eq.) in THF (10
mL/mmol) at -78 °C. After stirring for 1 h, a solution of InCl3 (1.0 eq.)
in THF (5 mL/mmol) was added. Stirring was continued for a further 30 min
before addition of the corresponding aldehyde (1.0 eq.). After 1 h, the
reaction mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature before addition
of 1.0 M aq. HCl solution (5 mL/mmol). The aqueous layer was extracted
with Et2O (10 mL/mmol × 2) and the combined organic layers were washed
with water (10mL/mmol) and sat. aq. NaCl solution (10 mL/mmol) and dried
over Na2SO4. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the
crude product was purified by flash column chromatography to give the
corresponding alcohol as a mixture of diastereoisomers which were not
separated. (1RS,2RS) and
(1RS,2SR)-2-Butoxy-3-methyl-1-phenylbut-3-en-1-ol 9 Benzaldehyde (102 μL,
1.00 mmol) was subjected to general procedure A using 1-(2-
methylallyloxy)butane 8, and was purified by flash column chromatography
(12:1 petrol:ether) to give alcohol 9 as a colourless oil (201 mg, 86%)
and a mixture of diastereoisomers which were not separated (ca. 5:1 from
1H NMR). The 1H and 13C NMR data provided is for the major
diastereoisomer. νmax (thin film)/cm-1 3553br s, 2959s, 2872s, 1649s,
1496s, 1454s, 1377s, 1331s, 1196s, 1092s, 1012s, 904s, 822s; δH (400.2
MHz, CDCl3) 0.95 (3H, t, J 7.5, C(4')H3), 1.36-1.48 (2H, m, C(3')H2),
1.57-1.65 (2H, m, C(2')H2), 1.59 (3H, s, Me), 3.28 (1H, dt, 9.0, 6.5,
C(1')H), 3.37 (1H, d, J 1.0, OH), 3.50 (1H, dt, J 9.0, 6.5, C(1')H), 3.65
(1H, d, J 8.0, C(2)H), 4.60 (1H, dd, J 8.0, 1.0, C(1)H), 4.68-4.70 (1H,
m, C(4)H), 4.84-4.86 (1H, m, C(4)H), 7.24-7.42 (5H, m, Ph); δC (100.6
MHz, CDCl3) 13.9 (C(4')), 18.1 (Me), 19.4 (C(3')), 31.9 (C(2')), 68.5
(C(1')), 75.5 (C(1)), 88.9 (C(2)), 116.0 (C(4)), 127.2 (Ph), 127.8 (Ph),
128.0 (Ph), 139.9 and 141.2 (C(3), i-Ph); m/z 257 (100%, MNa+); HRMS
(ESI) C15H22NaO2 (MNa+) requires 257.1512, found 257.1507 (+1.87 ppm)
