$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-Hydroxy-3-(4-methoxyphenyl)-2-methylenepropanenitrile (19i).
Purification by column chromatography (3:1 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a
desired compound 19i (187 mg, 98%) as a yellow liquid. Spectral data were
identical to those previously reported.11 TLC: R f 0.17 (3:1
hexane/EtOAc). 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.31 (d, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 6.92
(d, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 6.12 (d, 1H, J = 1.6 Hz), 6.03 (d, 1H, J = 1.6 Hz),
5.28 (m, 1H), 3.82 (s, 3H), 2.26 (d, 1H, J = 4.0 Hz). 13C-NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 160.3, 131.6, 129.6, 128.2, 126.6, 117.2, 114.6, 74.0, 55.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction, 1-butyl-3-methyltriazolium hexafluorophosphate
as solvent gave similar yield
