$DATUM (E)-1-(4-Methoxybenzyloxy)dec-3-en-6-yn-5-ol (27). To a solution of
1-pentyne (0.64 mL, 6.5 mmol, 1.3 equiv) in THF (12 mL) at -40 °C was
added a solution of n-BuLi (2.4 mL, 2.5 M in hexanes, 6.0 mmol, 1.2
equiv). After 10 min stirring at 0 °C, the resulting pent-1-ynyllithium
solution was cooled to -40 °C and a solution of aldehyde 26 (1.10 g, 4.99
mmol) in THF (8 mL) was added dropwise. After 1.5 h from 0 °C to rt, the
reaction mixture was poured into a saturated aqueous solution of NH4Cl.
The layers were separated and the aqueous phase was extracted with Et2O.
The combined organic extracts were dried over MgSO4, filtered and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude material was purified by
flash chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether/EtOAc gradient: 80/20
to 70/30) to afford alcohol 27. Yellow oil, yield 1.41 g, 98%. IR 3385,
1612, 1586, 1512, 1462, 1361, 1301, 1245, 1173, 1086, 1031, 966, 819, 736
cm-1; 1H NMR δ 7.28-7.23 (m, 2H), 6.89-6.86 (m, 2H), 5.87 (dtd, J = 15.3
Hz, J = 6.8 Hz and J = 1.2 Hz, 1H), 5.67 (ddt, J = 15.3 Hz, J = 6.0 Hz
and J = 1.4 Hz, 1H), 4.82 (m, 1H), 4.44 (s, 2H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 3.50 (t, J
= 6.8 Hz, 2H), 2.37 (dtd, apparent qt, J = 6.8 Hz and J = 1.0 Hz, 2H),
2.21 (apparent td, J = 7.0 Hz and J = 2.0 Hz, 2H), 2.02 (br s, 1H), 1.54
(apparent sextuplet, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 0.98 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR δ
159.1 (s), 131.4 (d), 130.4 (s), 129.5 (d), 129.3 (d, 2C), 113.7 (d, 2C),
86.7 (s), 79.6 (s), 72.5 (t), 69.0 (t), 63.0 (d), 55.2 (q), 32.3 (t),
22.0 (t), 20.7 (t), 13.5 (q). HRMS calcd for C18H24O3Na (M+Na+):
311.16177. Found: 311.16151. C18H24O3; Mol. Wt.: 288,38.
