$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure of Enantioselective Aldol
Reaction: Preparation of
2,3-Dihydro-2-(hydroxycyclohexylmethyl)-1H-inden-1-one (3i). To a stirred
solution of (R)-3,3’-dibromo-1,1'-binaphthalene-2,2'-diol (21.0 mg, 0.047
mmol, 0.1 eq) in THF (3 mL) was added H2O in THF (2.8 M, 0.25 mL, 0.70
mmol, 1.5 eq) and n-butyllithium in hexane (0.16 M, 0.6 mL, 0.094 mmol,
0.2 eq) at -23 °C, and the mixture was stirred for a few minutes. To this
yellow mixture, a solution of cyclohexanecarbaldehyde in THF (1.0 M, 0.5
mL, 0.47 mmol) and 1-trimethoxysilyloxy-3H-indene (0.17 mL, 0.70 mmol,
1.5 eq) was added. The mixture was stirred for 0.5 h at the same
temperature and the reaction was quenched with KF/KH2PO4 aq (15% KF, 10%
KH2PO4 solution, 2 mL). The mixture was diluted with AcOEt (10 mL) and
washed with brine for 3 times. The organic layer was dried over Na2SO4,
and then evaporated. The crude product was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (CH2Cl2/hexane 8/1, then CH2Cl2/AcOEt 160/1→10/1).
2,3-Dihydro-2-(1-hydroxy-3-phenyl-2-propenyl)-1H-inden-1-one (3g). 1H NMR
δ 2.8-3.0 (m, 2H), 3.1-3.3 (m, 4H), 4.52 (t, 1H, J = 6.5 Hz, HC-OH anti),
5.02 (m, 1H, HC-OH syn), 6.2-6.3 (m, 2H), 6.7-6.8 (m, 2H), 7.2-7.8 (m,
18H). 13C NMR δ 27.3, 29.6, 52.0, 52.6, 71.6, 74.0, 123.8, 124.1, 126.4,
126.5, 126.6, 127.3, 127.6, 127.7, 127.8, 128.5, 128.7, 129.4, 131.0,
132.2, 135.0, 135.4, 136.3, 136.3, 136.4, 137.0, 154.0, 154.8, 207.8,
209.0 (syn/anti mixture). [α]D 25 +82.2 (c 0.96, CHCl3) (syn : anti = 3.4
: 1) IR (KBr) 3478, 1698, 1605, 1464, 1329, 1296, 1205, 963, 765, 705.
LR-EIMS 264 (M+), 246, 132. HR-EIMS calcd for C18H16O2 264.1150, found
264.1158. HPLC (Daicel chiralpak AS-H, Hex/IPA = 9/1, 1.0 mL/min): t R
22.1 (anti-major), 26.8 (anti-minor), 31.8 (syn-minor), 37.2 min
(syn-major).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
