$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A. Aldol Addition of Acetic
Acid to Aldehydes. To an oven-dried 10-mL round-bottomed flask under N2
was added CH2Cl2 (5.0 mL), acetic acid (57 μL, 60 mg, 0.996 mmol),
i-Pr2NEt (435 μL, 323 mg, 2.50 mmol), aldehyde (1.4 mmol), and TMSOTf
(400 μL, 491 mg, 2.21 mmol). NOTE: addition of TMSOTf to the reaction
mixture produces a mildly exothermic reaction on this scale. The reaction
was stirred at room temperature, and the colorless solution became pale
yellow. After 2 h, the reaction mixture was added to a 25-mL
round-bottomed flask with 10 mL EtOH (95%) and 5-10 drops trifluoroacetic
acid. The reaction mixture was concentrated by rotary evaporation. Flash
chromatography (10-50% EtOAc/hex). The pure product.
3-Hydroxy-3-(2-furyl)propanoic acid (5) When General Procedure A was
followed using 2-furaldehyde (115 μL, 133 mg, 1.39 mmol), the title
compound was prepared as a brown oil (80% yield). IR (film) 3115, 2914,
2650, 1714, 1491, 1410, 1149,1005, 740 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, Acetone) δ
7.48 (dd, J = 0.9, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 6.37 (dd, J = 1.7, 3.4 Hz, 1H), 6.32 (ap
d, J = 3.4 Hz, 1H), 5.12 (dd, J = 5.5, 8.0 Hz, 1H), 2.86-2.76 (m, 2H);
13C NMR (125 MHz, Acetone) δ 171.4, 156.7, 141.8, 110.1, 105.5, 63.8,
40.3; HRMS (ESI): Exact mass calcd for C7H8O4Na [M+Na]+, 179.0315. Found
179.0309.
