$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure I. Pyridine N-Oxide
Catalyzed Additions of tert-Butyl isocyanide A solution of tert-butyl
isocyanide (1.2 equiv, 1.0 M in CH2Cl2) was added to a solution of an
aldehyde (1.0 M in CH2Cl2 based on aldehyde), pyridine N-oxide (0.1
equiv), and SiCl4 (1.1 equiv) at -74 °C over 30 min via a syringe pump.
After being stirred for the indicated time, the reaction mixture was
warmed to rt and transferred dropwise to a vigorously stirred, ice-cold,
saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (20 mL). The mixture was further
stirred for 2 h at rt. The white precipitate was filtered off through
Celite and the filtrate was extracted with CH2Cl2 (4 x 20 mL). The
combined organic layers were dried (MgSO4) and concentrated under reduced
pressure. Pyridine N-oxide was separated from the product by silica gel
chromatography (hexane/EtOAc). Analytically pure product was obtained
after recrystallization (heptane/benzene).
N-tert-Butyl-2-hydroxy-4-phenyl-3-ene-butenamide ((±)-5g) Following
General Procedure I, a mixture of trans-cinnamaldehyde 3g (126 μL, d =
1.048, 1.0 mmol), pyridine N-oxide (9.5 mg, 0.1 mmol, 0.1 equiv), SiCl4
(125 μL, d = 1.483, 1.1 mmol, 1.1 equiv), and tert-butyl isocyanide (125
μL, d = 0.735, 1.2 mmol, 1.2 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL) was stirred for 4
h at -74 °C. After work-up and silica gel chromatography (20 mm column,
60 g SiO2, Rf 0.26, hexane/EtOAc, 2/1), 170 mg (73%) of (±)-5g was
obtained as an off-white solid. White crystals of (±)-5g (132 mg, 57%)
were obtained after recrystallization from a 3/1 mixture of heptane and
benzene. Data for (±)-5g: mp: 93-94°C (heptane/benzene, 3/1) 1H NMR: (400
MHz, CDCl3) 7.27-7.42 (m, 5 H, aryl); 6.74 (d, J = 15.9, 1 H, HC(4));
6.25 (dd, J = 15.8, 3.0, 1 H, HC(3)); 5.95 (bs, 1 H, NH); 4.58 (d, J =
6.8, 1 H, HC(2)); 3.41 (bs, 1 H, OH); 1.37 (s, 9 H, 3 X H3C(2'')) 13C
NMR: (100 MHz, CDCl3) 170.9 (C(1)), 136.0 (C(1')), 133.3 (C(4)), 128.6
(C(3')), 128.1 (C(3)), 127.2 (C(4')), 126.7 ((C(2')), 73.0 (C(2)), 51.5
(C(1'')), 28.7 (C(2'')) IR: (CHCl3) 3614 (m), 3413 (m), 3006 (m), 2973
(m), 2935 (m), 1678 (s), 1521 (s), 1456 (m), 1394 (w), 1367 (m), 1276
(w), 1236 (w), 1216 (w), 1108 (m), 1072 (w), 968 (m) TLC: Rf 0.26
(hexane/EtOAc, 2/1) SFC: (S)-5g, tR 2.35 min (50.2%); (R)-5g, tR 2.77 min
(49.8%) (Chiracel AD, 10.0% MeOH in CO2, 125 bar, 40 °C, 3.0 mL min-1)
MS: (FI, 70 eV) 234 (16), 233 (100), 232 (3), 231 (16), 207 (3), 148 (2)
Analysis: C14H19NO2 (233.31) Calcd: C, 72.07; H, 8.21; N, 6.00% Found: C,
71.91; H, 8.23; N, 6.06%
