$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of
(S,E)-(5-(allyloxy)-5-(naphthalen-2-yl)pent-3-enyloxy)(tert-butyl)dimethylsilane
(S)-11(E)-5-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-1-(naphthalen-2-yl)pent-2-en-1-ol
(S5) To a cooled (-80 °C) solution of 2-bromonaphthalene (3.83 g, 18.5
mmol) in THF (95 mL) was added dropwise a solution of t-BuLi (1.45 M in
pentane, 25.5 mL) over 15 min. The solution was stirred at the same
temperature for 15 min before addition of S43(3.6 g, 16.8 mmol) in THF (8
mL). After warming to -60 °C, the mixture was diluted with 10% aqueous
NH4Cl solution (100 mL), and extracted with Et2O (50 mL x 2). Combined
organic phases were washed with saturated brine (100 mL), dried and
concentrated. The residual oil was subjected to column chromatography
(silica gel 200 g, elution with hexane:AcOEt = 5:1) to give S5 (4.60 g,
80% (Chiralpak IA, hexane:EtOH = 200:1, flow rate 1.0 mL/min, detection
at 254 nm, tr = 22.89 min and 24.95 min)). a colarless oil, Rf = 0.43
(hexane:AcOEt = 3:1).
(E)-5-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-1-(naphthalen-2-yl)pent-2-en-1-ol
(S5), Yield (4.60 g, 80%) IR (film) 3390, 2953, 2930, 2857 cm-1. 1H 1H
NMR (CDCl3) δ -0.04 and 0.04 (each 3H, s, SiMe2Bu), 0.87 (9H, s, t-Bu),
2.06 (1H, brs, -OH), 2.28-2,32 (2H, m, H-4), 3.65 (1H, t, J = 9.4 Hz,
H-5), 5.33 (1H, brs, H-1), 5.80-5.82 (2H, m, H-2, H-3), 7.46-7.48 (3H, m,
naphthyl), 7.81-7.83 (4H, m, naphthyl). 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ -5.1 (SiMe2),
18.4 (CMe3), 26.1 (SiMe2Bu), 36.0 (C-4), 62.9 (C-5), 76.9 (C-1), 129.5
and 134.3 (C-2 and C-3), 124.7, 124.8, 126.0, 126.3, 127.9, 128.2, 128.4,
133.2, 133.6, 140.8 (phenyl). HRMS calcd for C12H30O2Si (M+) 342.2015,
found 342.2018.
