$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Enantio- and Diastereoselective Vinyl
Additions to Aldehydes. General Procedure. An oven-dried 10 mL Schlenk
flask that had been thoroughly purged with N2 was charged with trisvinyl
borane (0.4 equiv, 0.4 M in toluene) and cooled to - 10 °C. Me2Zn (1.4
equiv, 2 M in toluene) was added dropwise over 10 min and allowed to
stirred at this temperature for 10 min before the addition of (−)-MIB (4
mol%). The reaction was warmed to 0 °C and a solution of aldehyde (1
equiv, 1 M in toluene) was added over 30 min with the aid of a syringe
pump. The reaction was allowed to stir at this temperature for 12 hours
and was quenched with ~100 μL H2O. After stirring for 15 min, MgSO4 was
added followed by 5 mL of diethyl ether.The resulting suspension was
filtered, and successively washed with diethyl ether (~5 mL × 2). The
organic layer was concentrated and chromatographed on silica gel that had
been pretreated with triethylamine (2.5% v/v Et3N) to afford the desired
product . 3-Ethoxy-1-naphthalen-2-yl-prop-2-en-1-ol (S4). The General
Procedure was applied to 2-naphthaldehyde on 1 mmol (156 mg, 1 M in
toluene) scale. The crude product was purified by column chromatography
on silica gel that had been pretreated with triethylamine (2.5% v/v Et3N,
20% ethyl acetate in hexanes) to afford the desired product as colorless
oil (212 mg, 93% yield). colorless oil. [α]D 20 = +18.2 (c 0.69, MeOH);
1H NMR (C6D6, 500 MHz): δ 0.98 (t, 3H, J = 7 Hz), 1.62 (br, 1H), 3.28 (m,
2H), 4.98 (dd, 1H, J = 12.5 and 8.2 Hz ), 5.06 (d, 1H, J = 8.2 Hz), 6.46
(d, 1H, J = 12.4 Hz), 7.25 (m, 2H), 7.51 (d, 1H, J = 8.5 Hz), 7.61-7.69
(m, 3H), and 7.89 (s, 1H) ppm. 13C{1H} NMR (C6D6, 125 MHz): δ 14.6, 64.5,
72.7, 107.0, 124.7, 125.1, 125.9, 126.3, 128.0, 128.3, 128.4, 133.0,
134.0, 142.5, and 149.2 ppm. IR (neat): IR 3401, 3053, 2977, 1667, 1634,
1601, 1505, and 1477 cm-1. HRMS calcd for C15H16O2 (M)+: 228.1150, found
228.1156.
