$DATUM 3-(4-Chlorophenyl)-3-hydroxy-2-methylenepropanenitrile (19a).
Purification by column chromatography (3:1 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a
desired compound 19a (196 mg, 99%) as a colorless liquid. Spectral data
were identical to those previously reported.6 TLC: R f 0.21 (3:1
hexane/EtOAc). 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.39 (AB quartet, 2H, J = 8.8
Hz), 7.35 (AB quartet, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 6.13 (d, 1H, J = 1.6 Hz), 6.06
(d, 1H, J = 1.6 Hz), 5.32 (m, 1H), 2.30 (d, 1H, J = 4.0 Hz). 13C-NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ 137.8, 135.1, 130.3, 129.3, 128.1, 126.1, 116.9, 73.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction, 1-butyl-3-methyltriazolium hexafluorophosphate
as solvent gave similar yield
