$DATUM 3-(4-Fluorophenyl)-3-hydroxy-2-methylenepropanenitrile (19b).
Purification by column chromatography (3:1 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a
desired compound 19b (177 mg, 99%) as a pale-yellow liquid. Spectral data
were identical to those previously reported.7 TLC: R f 0.20 (3:1
hexane/EtOAc). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.39 (dd, 2H, J = 8.4, 5.2 Hz),
7.10 (t, 2H, J = 8.4 Hz), 6.13 (d, 1H, J = 1.2 Hz), 6.06 (d, 1H, J = 1.2
Hz), 5.32 (d, 1H, J = 4.0 Hz), 2.31 (d, 1H, J = 4.0 Hz). 13C-NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ 163.1 (d, JCF = 246.4 Hz), 135.2 (d, JCF = 2.8 Hz), 130.2,
128.5 (d, JCF = 8.4 Hz), 126.3, 117.0, 116.0 (d, JCF = 21.7 Hz), 73.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction, 1-butyl-3-methyltriazolium hexafluorophosphate
as solvent gave similar yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 1,3-Dialkyl-1,2,3-triazolium Ionic Liquids and Their
Applications to the Baylis-Hillman Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Jeong, Yunkyung; Ryu, Jae-Sang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2010), 75(12), 4183-4191

