$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Allylboration of aldehyde S4. To a solution of aldehyde S4 (836.5 mg, 5.0
mmol, 1.0 equiv) in anhydrous ether (25 mL) was added fresh prepared
(+)-diisopinocampheylallylborane (20 mL, 0.3 M in pentane, 6.0 mmol, 1.2
equiv) at -100 °C. [(+)-Diisopinocampheylallylborane in pentane was
prepared from (-)-B-chlorodiisopinocampheylborane (2.57 g, 8.0 mol) and
allyllmagnesium bromide (7.5 mL, 1 M solution in ether, 7.5 mmol)
according to the method described for the synthesis of 10 4.] After the
addition was complete, the mixture was stirred at the same temperature
for 1 h. Methanol (1 mL) was added at -100 °C, and the reaction mixture
was allowed to warm to room temperature. Aminoethanol (0.91mL, 15.0 mmol,
3.0 equiv) was added. After being stirred overnight, saturated aqueous
NH4Cl solution (20 mL) was added. The mixture was extracted with EtOAc (3
x 20 mL), and the combined organics were dried over MgSO4, and
concentrated under reduced pressure followed by flash column
chromatography (gradient eluents, 10/1 →1/1, hexanes/ethyl acetate)
provided allylic alcohol intermediate (1.02 g, 97%) as a colorless oil.
Rf = 0.43 (hexanes/ethyl acetate, 1/1); [α]22 D -19.4 (c 1.0, CHCl3),
lit.11 -20.2 (c 1.0, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.94 (s, 1 H,
SCH=C), 6.56 (s, 1 H, CH=CCH3), 5.77-5.88 (m, 1 H, CH=CH2), 5.11-5.19 (m,
2 H, CH=CH 2), 4.22 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 1 H, CHOH), 2.71 (s, 3H, N=C(S)CH3),
2.35-2.47 (m, 2 H, CH2=CHCH 2), 2.05 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 3H, CH=CCH 3), 1.90
(d, J = 2.8 Hz, 1H, OH); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 164.80, 152.89,
141.70, 134.82, 119.17, 117.94, 115.62, 76.61, 40.15, 19.28, 14.51. The
analytical data are in agreement with those reported in the literature.11
