$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the synthesis of syn α-vinyl-β-hydroxy esters 3. To
a 0 °C solution of borohydride 6R (81 mg, 0.250 mmol, 1 equiv,
considering a 90% yield for the conversion of borohydride 6R to borane 1R
based on titration3) in CH2Cl2 (0.5 mL) was added TMSCl (32 μL, 0.250
mmol, 1 equiv). The reaction mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 10 min, then
a solution of allene ester 24 (0.325 mmol, 1.3 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL)
was added. The reaction mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 1h, then was
cooled to -78 °C and benzaldehyde (18 μL, 0.175 mmol, 0.7 equiv) was
added. The mixture was stirred at -78 °C for 12h before a pH 7 buffer
solution (KH2SO4/NaOH) (1 mL), THF (1.5 mL) and MeOH (0.5 mL) were added.
The heterogeneous solution was allowed to warm to 20 °C and was stirred
vigorously for 6h. The mixture was poured into a saturated aqueous NH4Cl
solution and was extracted with EtOAc (3x). The combined organic layers
were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated
under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by flash column
chromatography (SiO2, hexanes / EtOAc, gradient elution). syn
α-vinyl-β-hydroxy esters 3a-g. (R)-Ethyl
2-((R)-hydroxy(phenyl)methyl)but-3-enoate (3a). Colorless oil; Yield 86%;
syn/anti >40:1; ee 82%; [α]D 25 = + 75.2 (c 0.75, CHCl3); 1H (400 MHz,
CDCl3) 7.34-7.23 (m, 5H), 5.95 (ddd, J = 17.2, 10.1, 8.8, Hz, 1H), 5.25
(dd, J = 10.1, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 5.15 (dt, J = 17.2, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 4.99 (d, J =
6.1 Hz, 1H), 4.03 (q, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 3.31 (dd, J = 8.8, 6.1 Hz, 1H),
2.92 (s, 1H), 1.10 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H); 13C (100 MHz, CDCl3) 172.7,
140.8, 132.1, 128.4, 128.1, 126.7, 120.7, 74.1, 61.1, 58.5, 14.2; IR
(neat) 3479, 2982, 2931, 1729, 1638, 1454, 1392, 1370, 1321, 1244, 1177,
1083, 1027, 993, 924, 765, 700 cm-1; HRMS (EI) calcd for C13H16O3 [M]+
220.1099, found 220.1094.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (stage 2), stereoselective (stage 3), buffered solution
(KHSO4/NaOH in last stage), 82%ee, optimization study (based on solvent,
reaction time, concentration and borane reagent)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantio- and Diastereoselective Synthesis of syn-β-Hydroxy-α-vinyl
Carboxylic Esters via Reductive Aldol Reactions of Ethyl
Allenecarboxylate with 10-TMS-9-Borabicyclo[3.3.2]decane and DFT Analysis
of the Hydroboration Pathway
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kister, Jeremy; Ess, Daniel H.; Roush, William R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(21), 5436-5439

