$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The reaction of 2,3-dimehyl-1,3-butadiene or
isoprene with electrophiles A 10 mL of round bottom flask charged with
InCl3 (0.442 g, 2.0 mmol) was dried by heating at 110 °C under reduced
pressure (1 mmHg) for 1 h. After nitrogen was filled, THF (2 mL) was
added to dissolve InCl3. To the mixture was added Bu3SnH (2.0 mmol) at
-78 °C. The mixture was stirred for 10 min to prepare dichloroindium
hydride (HInCl2). After the solution was warmed up to rt, 1,3-diene (4.0
mmol) was added to the mixture and the resulting mixure was stirred for 5
h. Then electrophile (1.0 mmol) was added and stirred for 3 h. The
resulting mixture was quenched by 1N HCl aq (10 mL). (When imine was used
as electrophile the reaction was quenched by water.) The reaction mixture
was extracted with ether (10 mL x 3). The combined organic layer was
treated with NH4F aq and then precipitate was filtered to remove tin
compound. The filtrate was extracted with ether and dried over MgSO4.
Concentration followed by silica gel column chromatography eluting with
hexane/AcOEt = (9/1) affored product. Further Purification was performed
by distillation under reduced pressure or GPC. Product was determined by
1H NMR. 1-(4-Methoxy-phenyl)-2,2,3-trimethyl-but-3-en-1-ol (3e) Shape:
colorless liquid. bp 155 °C/ 0.7 mmHg IR (neat) 3537 (O-H) cm-1 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 7.24 (d, J= 8.7 Hz, 2H), 6.84 (d, J= 8.7 Hz, 2H), 5.00
(s, 1H), 4.94 (s, 1H), 4.57(s, 1H), 3.79 (s, 3H), 1.85 (s, 3H), 0.98 (s,
3H), 0.91 (s, 3H) 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 158.75, 150.69, 132.33,
128.92, 112.97, 112.74, 77.04, 55.11, 44.52, 24.15, 20.02, 19.81 MS (CI,
70 eV) m/z 221 (M+ + 1, 6), 203 (M+ -OH, 100), 137 (M+
-C(CH3)2C(CH3)=CH2, 31) HRMS calcd for C14H20O2 + H: 221.1542, found: m/z
221.1552 (CI, (M+ + H), + 1.0 mmu)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
