$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, stereoselective, benzoin reaction, caution:
liquid aldehydes often contain the corresponding carboxylic acids
generated by auto-oxidation, which may neutralize the base to hinder the
formation of NHC. When the solvent-free NHC-catalyzed reaction is
unsuccessful, it is highly recommended that the aldehydes are newly
purchased and carefully distilled. The solvent-free NHC-catalyzed
reaction is more sensitive to a trace amount of acid than the
corresponding reaction in organic solvent; under solvent-free conditions,
addition of a slightly excess amount of Cs2CO3 with respect to
precatalyst caused partial racemization, and addition of an excess amount
of Cs2CO3 with respect to precatalyst H resulted in a drop of the
conversion, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
