$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5: 1-(6-Chloropyridin-3-yl)prop-2-en-1-ol A solution of vinyl magnesium
bromide (100 mL, 100 mmol) in THF was added dropwise into another
solution of 4 (5.66 g, 40 mmol) in THF (300 mL) at 0 °C and the resulting
mixture was allowed to stir for 2 hours. When TLC has shown the full
depletion of the starting material 4, ammonium chloride (100 mL) was then
used to quench the reaction. The mixture was filtered and the filtrate
was then concentrated where ethyl acetate (5 x 100 mL) was used to
extract the aqueous layer. The combined extracts were washed with brine
(50 mL), dried (MgSO4) and evaporated in vacuo. The residual oil was
purified via flash column chromatography (10:1 hexane/ethyl acetate),
yielding 6.51 g (38.3 mmol, 96%) of the allylic alcohol 5 as a dark
yellow oil. 5: 1-(6-Chloropyridin-3-yl)prop-2-en-1-ol, yield 6.51 g (38.3
mmol, 96%) Rf = 0.43 (2:1 hexane/ethyl acetate); Rf = 0.43 (2:1
hexane/ethyl acetate); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.38 (d, J = 2.07 Hz,
1H), 7.68 (dd, J = 2.46, 8.37 Hz, 1H), 7.30 (d, J = 8.37 Hz, 1H), 5.99
(ddd, J = 3.83, 10.10, 17.07 Hz, 1H), 5.42 – 5.26 (m, 3H); 13C NMR (75.4
MHz, CDCl3): δ 150.6, 147.9, 139.1, 137.0, 136.9, 124.1, 116.7, 72.5;
FTIR (neat): 1648, 1583, 1459, 1377, 1106, 1025, 932, 825, 746 cm-1; HRMS
(ESI) Calcd for C8H8ClNO [M+]: 169.0294, found: 170.0373 (M + 1).
