$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: All reactions were carried out in water. TiCl3
(15%, 1.5mL), SnCl2 (20 mmol), ally halide (20 mmol), water (10~20 mL)
and aldehyde (18 mmol) were mixed in a flask. The mixture was stirred in
room temperature for several hours. The mixture was then extracted with
ether directly (3 × 30 mL). The combined organic layer was washed by
water several times until the aqueous layer became colorless. After this
operation, the organic layer which contains the crude product was dried
over anhydrous MgSO4 and the solvent was removed at low temperature. The
residue was usually pure enough for NMR analyses. From the weight
analyses the yield under this condition was calculated. In the cases when
the residue is not sufficiently pure, flash column chromatography was
used to purify it. Compound 14, yield 100% C10H10Cl2O IR: (cm-1) 3280,
3079, 1638, 1590, 1564, 1470, 1102, 1070. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ(ppm)
7.51 (d, J= 8.23 Hz, 1H), 7.35 (s, 1H), 7.27 (d, J= 8.5 Hz, 1H), 5.85 (m,
1H), 5.20 (d, J= 12.9 Hz, 2H), 5.12 (t, J= 4.44 Hz, 1H), 2.60 (m, 1H),
2.27 (m, 1H), 2.16 (br, 1H). 13C NMR (300M, CDCl3): δ(ppm) 139.9, 133.9,
133.5, 132.3, 129.1, 128.2, 127.4, 119.0, 69.3, 42.0 Elemental analysis:
Found: C 55.36%, H 4.66%; Calc: C 55.33%, H 4.64%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel Carbonyl Allylation Mediated by SnCl2/TiCl3 in Water
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tan, Xiang-Hui; Shen, Bo; Deng, Wei; Zhao, Hui; Liu, Lei; Guo, Qing-Xiang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2003), 5(11), 1833-1835

