$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of the α,β-unsaturated aldehyde 15 (77 mg, 0.42 mmol) and
(S)-(+)-DPMPM (21 mg, 0.08 mmol) in hexane (1.0 ml) cooled to 0 °C was
added diethylzinc (1.01 M solution in hexane, 0.92 ml, 0.92 mmol). After
stirring at 0 °C for 16 h, the mixture was diluted with Et2O and poured
into 1 M aqueous KHSO4 solution. The aqueous layer was extracted with
Et2O (3 times). The combined organic layer waswashed with saturated
aqueous NaHCO3, brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and then concentrated
under reduced pressure. The resulting residue was purified by silica gel
chromatography (1:5 AcOEt/hexane) to afford allyl alcohol 9 (83mg, 92%)
as a colorless oil. Diastereoslectivity was determined to be 93:7 by
acetylation of 9 and 1H NMR analysis of the resultant crude products:
(1E,3S)-1-[(4S,5S)-2,2-dimethyl-5-vinyl-1,3-dioxolan-4-yl]pent-1-en-3-ol
9: , yield (83mg, 92%) [α]D 19 = -37.8 (c 0.85, CHCl3); IR (NaCl) λmax
3433 cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 0.93 (3H, t, J = 7.5 Hz), 1.45 (6H,
s), 1.56 (2H, dqn, J = 7.5, 2.0 Hz) , 1.68 (1H, br), 4.06-4.14 (3H), 5.26
(1H, dq, J = 10.2, 0.7 Hz), 5.36 (1H, dt, J = 17.1, 1.2 Hz), 5.67 (1H,
ddd, J = 15.5, 6.8, 1.2 Hz), 5.75-5.87 (2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ
9.5, 26.95, 26.98, 29.9, 73.0, 81.4, 82.4, 109.1, 119.0, 126.0, 134.0,
137.8. Anal. Calcd for C12H20NO3: C, 67.89; H, 9.50. Found: C, 68.06; H,
9.90.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of (-)-Agelastatin A by [3.3] Sigmatropic Rearrangement of
Allyl Cyanate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
