$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Triethyl-hex-5-en-3-ynyloxy-sliane: To a
stirred solution of vinyl bromide (1.0 M solution of THF, 18 mL, 18.0
mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (208 mg, 0.18 mmol), CuI (91.6 mg, 0.48 mmol), and Et3N
(3.4 mL, 24.0 mmol) was added a solution of but-3-ynyloxy-triethylsilane
(2.21 g, 12.0 mmol) in THF (6 mL) via a syringe pump over 1 hour. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3 hours and then it
was filtered through Celite. The solvent was removed in vacuo.
Purification of residue by flash chromatography (SiO2: Rf = 0.72,
hexanes/EtOAc = 20/1) gave the enyne product.
3-Cyclohexyl-2-hydroxy-hexa-3,5-dienoic acid ethyl ester, yield 74%. 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): 6.71 (ddd, J = 10.1, 11.1, 16.8 Hz, 1H), 6.01 (d, J
= 11.1 Hz, 1H), 5.24 (dd, J = 16.8, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 5.18 (dd, J = 10.2, 1.2
Hz, 1H), 4.59 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1H), 4.23 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 3.03 (d, J =
6.0 Hz, 1H), 2.51 (m, 1H), 1.81-1.43 (m, 8H), 1.35-1.15 (m, 2H), 1.25 (t,
J = 7.2 Hz, 3H).13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): 174.2, 144.2, 132.1, 129.0,
119.0, 72.9, 61.8, 39.9, 31.9, 31.2, 26.7, 26.6, 25.9, 14.1.HRMS Calcd.
for C14H23O3 (M+1): 239.1647, Found: 239.1645. FTIR (neat): 3493, 2929,
2852, 1732, 1448, 1211, 1076, 1024, 988, 909 cm-1. HPLC (Chiralcel OD-H
column, 1% i-PrOH/hexanes, 0.4 mL/min, 254 nm), tmajor = 18.7 min, tminor
= 21.6 min; ee = 94%. [α]D = + 72.0 (c = 2.87, CH2Cl2).
