$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Enantio- and Diastereoselective Vinyl
Additions to Aldehydes. General Procedure. An oven-dried 10 mL Schlenk
flask that had been thoroughly purged with N2 was charged with trisvinyl
borane (0.4 equiv, 0.4 M in toluene) and cooled to - 10 °C. Me2Zn (1.4
equiv, 2 M in toluene) was added dropwise over 10 min and allowed to
stirred at this temperature for 10 min before the addition of (−)-MIB (4
mol%). The reaction was warmed to 0 °C and a solution of aldehyde (1
equiv, 1 M in toluene) was added over 30 min with the aid of a syringe
pump. The reaction was allowed to stir at this temperature for 12 hours
and was quenched with ~100 μL H2O. After stirring for 15 min, MgSO4 was
added followed by 5 mL of diethyl ether.The resulting suspension was
filtered, and successively washed with diethyl ether (~5 mL × 2). The
organic layer was concentrated and chromatographed on silica gel that had
been pretreated with triethylamine (2.5% v/v Et3N) to afford the desired
product . 3-Ethoxy-1-(2-methoxy-phenyl)-prop-2-en-1-ol (S2). The General
Procedure was applied to ortho-methoxybenzaldehyde on 1.0 mmol (136 mg, 1
M in toluene) scale. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel that had been pretreated with triethylamine
(2.5 % v/v Et3N, 20 % ethyl acetate in hexanes) to afford the desired
product as colorless oil (204 mg, 98 % yield). colorless oil. [α]D 20 =
−32.4 (c = 0.85, MeOH); 1H NMR (C6D6, 500 MHz): δ 0.96 (t, 3H, J = 7.0
Hz), 2.44 (br, 1H), 3.24 (s, 3H), 3.25-3.37 (m, 2H), 5.17 (dd, 1H, J =
12.7 and 7.7 Hz ), 5.53 (d, 1H, J = 7.7 Hz), 6.51 (d, 1H, J = 8.2 Hz),
6.92 (td, 1H, J = 6.1 and 1.0 Hz), 7.08 (td, 1H, J = 8.0 and 1.7 Hz), and
7.55 (dd, 1H, J = 7.5 and 1.7 Hz) ppm. 13C{1H} NMR (C6D6, 125 MHz): δ
14.7, 54.8, 64.3, 68.6, 106.8, 110.7, 121.1, 127.3, 128.3, 133.5, 148.8,
and 157.1 ppm. IR (neat): 3442, 1651, 1600, 1489, 1487, and 1464 cm-1.
HRMS calcd for C12H16O3 (M)+: 208.1086, found 208.1089
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalytic Asymmetric Synthesis of Hydroxy Enol Ethers: Approach to a
Two-Carbon Homologation of Aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
