$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-((2-Chlorophenyl)(hydroxy)methyl)pent-1-en-3-one (34). To a stirred
solution of 2-chlorobenzaldehyde (113 μL, 141.0 mg, 1.00 mmol) in DMF
(900 μL) and water (100 μL), ethyl vinyl ketone (297 μL, 252.4 mg, 3.00
mmol), rac-proline (12.1 mg, 0.105 mmol), and NaHCO3 (21 mg, 0.25 mmol)
were added. The solution was allowed to stir for 5 days at room
temperature. The mixture was diluted with water (20 mL) and extracted
with CH2Cl2 (3 × 25 mL). The combined organic layers were dried (Na2SO4),
and the solvent evaporated under reduced pressure. The product was
purified by FC eluting with PE/EtOAc (9/1). Yield: (0.300 mmol, 67.4 mg,
30%), colorless oil. MS/CI (isobutane): [M-H]+ 225. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ
7.57-7.17 (m, 4H, ArH), 6.16 (d, 1H, J = 0.7 Hz,C═CH), 5.98 (d, 1H, J =
4.4 Hz, CH), 5.63 (d, 1H, J = 0.7 Hz,C═CH), 3.56 (d, 1H, J = 4.6 Hz, OH),
2.77 (q, 2H, J = 7.3 Hz, OCH2), 1.11 (t, 3H, J = 7.3 Hz, CH3). 13C NMR
(CDCl3): δ 203.1, 148.2, 138.8, 132.5, 129.4, 129.3, 128.0, 126.9, 125.9,
68.8, 31.4, 8.1. Anal. (C12H13ClO2) C, H. Elemental analysis: Formula:
C12H13ClO2. Calculated: C: 64.15%, H: 5.83%. Found: C: 64.33%, H: 6.03%.
cLogP: 2.23. TC50: 1.9 ± 8.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, Morita-Baylis-Hillman reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Electrophilic Warhead-Based Design of Compounds Preventing NLRP3
Inflammasome-Dependent Pyroptosis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cocco, Mattia; Garella, Davide; Di Stilo, Antonella; Borretto, Emily;
Stevanato, Livio; Giorgis, Marta; Marini, Elisabetta; Fantozzi, Roberto;
Miglio, Gianluca; Bertinaria, Massimo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Medicinal Chemistry (2014), 57(24), 10366-10382

