$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Asymmetric
Hydrocyanation Hydrocyanation of benzaldehyde (1a) is described as a
typical reaction procedure. Caution: (CH3)3SiCN and HCN must be used in a
well-ventilated hood due to their high toxicity. A 100-mL Schlenk tube
equipped with a Teflon-coated magnetic stirring bar was charged with a
bimetallic complex (S,S,S)-4a (10.8 mg, 10.1 μmol). After replacing the
air in the flask with argon, anhydrous CH3OH (481 mg, 15.0 mmol) was
placed in the flask, and the mixture was cooled down to 0 °C. To the
clear yellow solution was added (CH3)3SiCN (1.48 g, 14.9 mmol) in a
dropwise manner, and the resulting solution was stirred for 15 min.
Anhydrous t-C4H9OCH3 (38 mL) was placed in the flask, and the mixture was
cooled down to −78 °C. Then 1a (530 mg, 4.99 mmol) was added to the
solution, and the reaction mixture was stirred for 18 h. After the
solvent and the volatile compounds were evaporated under reduced pressure
at ambient temperature, the residue was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (eluent, n-hexane/ethyl acetate/trifluoroacetic acid =
70/30/0.1, ). (S)-2-Hydroxy-2-(2-furyl)acetonitrile [(S)-2m]. 89%
(isolated yield), brown oil, 92% ee. Solvent system for column
chromatography: n-hexane/ethyl acetate/trifluoroacetic acid =
100/10/0.1→80/20/0.1. [α]D 25 +42.0 degcm3g−1dm−1 (c 1.09 gcm−3, CHCl3);
lit.[4] [α]D +14.0 degcm3g−1dm−1 (c 1.87 gcm−3, CHCl3), 79% ee (S). IR
(KBr-neat) 3395, 2255, 1499, 1233, 1148, 1016, 958, 898, 881, 823, 748
cm−1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.93 (brs, 1H, OH), 5.55 (s, 1H, CHCN),
6.43 (dd, 1H, J = 1.6 and 3.2 Hz, aromatic H), 6.62 (d, 1H, J = 3.2 Hz,
aromatic H), 7.49−7.50 (m, 1H, aromatic H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
56.9 (CH), 110.2 (CH), 110.9 (CH), 116.9 (C), 144.4 (CH), 147.4 (C). HRMS
(ESI−) m/z calcd for C6H5 35ClNO2: 158.00088 ([M+35Cl]−); found:
158.00046. Chiral HPLC analysis: column, Daicel CHIRALPAK IC; eluent,
n-hexane/2-propanol/acetic acid = 97/3/0.1; flow rate, 1.0 mLmin−1;
column temp, 40 °C; detection, UV 220 nm;; tR of (S)-2m, 23.1 min
(95.8%); tR of (R)-2m, 27.7 min (4.2 %).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM safety, stereoselective (92% ee), dropwise addition of TMSCN stage 1
