$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(3):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (E, 2S,
3S,)-1,7-Bis-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-2,5-dimethyl-4-hepten-3-ol
(11a). A. Standard Procedure for Lithiation/Transmetallation of Vinyl
Iodide 6: To a magnetically stirred solution of vinyl iodide 6 (0.298 g,
0.914 mmol) in Et2O (2 mL) at -78 °C was added t-BuLi (1.7M in pentane,
1.2 mL, 2.04 mmol). The mixture was stirred for 15 min and then a
solution of ZnBr2 (0.89M in Et2O, 1.10 mL, 0.979 mmol, prepared by
dissolving 5 g of commercial ZnBr2 in 25 mL of Et2O with sonication) was
added dropwise by syringe. The mixture was warmed to 0 °C and stirred for
1 h. Then a solution of the lithium alkoxide of (1S,2R)-N-methylephedrine
(0.20M in toluene, 5.0 mL, 1.00 mmol) was added dropwise. The resulting
mixture was stirred for 1 h at 0 °C before aldehyde 9a (0.076 g, 0.376
mmol) in toluene (1 mL) was added dropwise. The reaction mixture was
stirred for 1 h and then was quenched by the addition of NH4Cl. The
aqueous layer was extracted with ether and the combined extracts were
washed with Na2S2O3, brine, dried over MgSO4, concentrated under vacuum
and chromatographed on silica gel (hexanes to 2.5% EtOAc-hexanes) to
afford alcohol 11a as a light yellow oil (0.106 g, 70%, 92 : 8 mixture of
syn and anti diastereomers): C. Without N-methylephedrine: The standard
procedure for vinyl iodide lithiation was employed with vinyl iodide 6
(0.302 g, 0.925 mmol), ZnBr2 (0.89M in Et2O, 1.10 mL, 0.979 mmol) and
aldehyde 12b (0.60 g, 0.365 mmol), affording alcohol 14b (0.110 g, 82%
yield, 95 : 5 mixture of syn and anti diastereomers) as a clear oil. All
analytical data was consistent with the N-methylephedrine directed cases.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative reaction conditions shown, anti:syn=5:95,
in-situ generated reactant
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diastereoselective Additions of Chiral Vinylzinc Reagents to α-Chiral
Aldehydes
